A classic example at the beginning of learning programming.
`hello.c` is the source file.

@[hello.c@=
@<hello@:executable@:C Structure@/module@>
@

@<hello@:executable@:C Structure@/main body@=
printf("Hello World!\n");
@~ output @
The command has a single usage without options or arguments.
@<hello@:executable@:Invocation@/invocation syntax@=
{
    name: 'hello',
}
@
